{
  "name": "customer-data-bucket",
  "description": "Example 2 (who can read the customer data bucket). Reading acme-customer-pii takes bucket access and the pii-key together. 44 people can: the 31 in eng-oncall (OncallRole, then DataAdminRole or BreakGlassRole), carol in data-science (AnalystRole through the analytics-ap access point), and 12 GitHub engineers in data-eng (they can push to etl-pipeline, whose OIDC trust gives DeployRole, which can update the nightly-export Lambda that runs as etl-lambda-role). The vendor account can too, through VendorSyncRole. svc-reporting (through the etl-writers group) and svc-etl reach the bucket by policy but hold no key grant, so they can't read it. Key access comes from decrypt grants: 'encrypted with' only says which key the bucket uses. Reduced: the example's aggregated members are listed by name. GitHub nodes use the stand-in entity.source github (Kibana has no GitHub entity source).",
